      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p34.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Exactly, \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\frac13-\\frac{33333333}{10^8}\\\\ =\\frac{10^8-3(33333333)} {3\\cdot10^8}\\\\ =\\frac1{3\\cdot10^8}. \\end{gathered} \\] Thus \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) is greater by the stated amount.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(0.33333333\\) as \\(\\frac{33333333}{10^8}\\)",
        "Subtract this terminating decimal from \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) using the denominator \\(3\\cdot10^8\\)"
      ],
